86
00:05:24,960 --> 00:05:37,680
Shall we Scoutmastership in seven minutes or less.

87
00:05:37,680 --> 00:05:45,520
We did a recent survey that was trying to look into meeting and outing attendance for Scouts.

88
00:05:45,520 --> 00:05:47,720
What encouraged them to come to meetings?

89
00:05:47,720 --> 00:05:52,080
What kind of- you know- complimentary, conflicting things that they have that cause them not

90
00:05:52,080 --> 00:05:53,920
to get to meetings or outings?

91
00:05:53,920 --> 00:05:58,080
And one of the things that was mentioned as a real attractant for both meetings

92
00:05:58,080 --> 00:06:00,240
and outings was fun,

93
00:06:00,240 --> 00:06:01,240
Fun.

94
00:06:01,240 --> 00:06:03,520
Well, everybody wants to have fun.

95
00:06:03,520 --> 00:06:06,360
Cindy Lauper said best girls just want to have fun.

96
00:06:06,360 --> 00:06:08,320
Why not boys?

97
00:06:08,320 --> 00:06:09,880
You know what?

98
00:06:09,880 --> 00:06:14,680
I think fun is something that we really need to have in Scouts.

99
00:06:14,680 --> 00:06:19,600
I think that we also need to really understand what that means.

100
00:06:19,600 --> 00:06:24,960
So fun means, in my experience, about three things.

101
00:06:24,960 --> 00:06:27,680
You know this is just hey. we're just talking here.

102
00:06:27,680 --> 00:06:29,120
This isn't science.

103
00:06:29,120 --> 00:06:33,800
I'm just telling you from my experience. these three things are important for fun

104
00:06:33,800 --> 00:06:41,920
And before we talk about them, I want you to start thinking like a 12 year old for just

105
00:06:41,920 --> 00:06:42,920
a little while.

106
00:06:42,920 --> 00:06:46,840
Go way back, do what you need to do, sit down in a quiet place,

107
00:06:46,840 --> 00:06:53,640
Think about you know your time as a 12 year old and think about what motivated you and

108
00:06:53,640 --> 00:06:56,280
what seemed to be fun to you.

109
00:06:56,280 --> 00:07:00,000
So once I've got you in that frame of mind, this makes a little more sense.

110
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:04,280
So for our Scouts, friends are fun.

111
00:07:04,280 --> 00:07:07,440
Scouts are really strongly motivated to hang out with their friends.

112
00:07:07,440 --> 00:07:09,800
I mean, it's a primal instinct.

113
00:07:09,800 --> 00:07:11,480
Do you remember this? as a kid,

114
00:07:11,480 --> 00:07:13,760
I remember we would cut classes.

115
00:07:13,760 --> 00:07:17,320
I'm not encouraging that activity,

116
00:07:17,320 --> 00:07:23,080
But you know we would. we risked an awful lot to be able to hang out with our friends.

117
00:07:23,080 --> 00:07:27,360
You know, if it came to cutting classes, going to class or being able to hang out

118
00:07:27,360 --> 00:07:33,000
with your friends, oh, every once in a while we would cut a class.

119
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:38,680
If we had to spin a tail to tell our parents so that we could all go hang out

120
00:07:38,680 --> 00:07:43,000
somewhere together, that's what we would do.

121
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:47,760
So it's a really powerful, instinctive thing. hanging out, just kind of being

122
00:07:47,760 --> 00:07:50,440
around and doing things with your friends,

123
00:07:50,440 --> 00:07:52,960
That's fun.

124
00:07:52,960 --> 00:07:57,080
Even school can be fun if you get to sit next to your friends or even if you

125
00:07:57,080 --> 00:07:58,960
just share a class with them.

126
00:07:58,960 --> 00:08:03,320
I mean boys, we'll go to a lot of trouble and potentially make a lot of trouble

127
00:08:03,320 --> 00:08:04,960
to be able to hang out with their friends.

128
00:08:04,960 --> 00:08:11,039
So let's think of that as part of the equation of fun.

129
00:08:11,039 --> 00:08:18,320
The other interesting thing is- and it didn't come to me like really fast-

130
00:08:18,320 --> 00:08:24,840
It took a long time before I realized that challenge is fun, especially for Scouts.

131
00:08:24,880 --> 00:08:29,520
I mean any kind of a physical challenge, from a 15-minute game to a five-day

132
00:08:29,520 --> 00:08:33,720
backpacking trip, is fun,

133
00:08:33,720 --> 00:08:39,320
And the more challenging the circumstances, the more fun everybody seems to have,

134
00:08:39,320 --> 00:08:41,800
at least in retrospect.

135
00:08:41,800 --> 00:08:45,080
So what are some fun things that we've done?

136
00:08:45,080 --> 00:08:50,320
Well, how about being huddled under a tarp for hours at the end of a

137
00:08:50,320 --> 00:08:57,720
portage trail up in Canada in this really intense, swirling electrical storm.

138
00:08:57,720 --> 00:09:04,000
It wasn't like the most pleasant thing to do, but, man, it was fun.

139
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:09,120
How about slogging up five miles of switchbacks with aching feet and an aching

140
00:09:09,120 --> 00:09:17,760
back and just swimming in sweat and having many more miles to go after?

141
00:09:17,760 --> 00:09:20,360
when you got over the top of that mountain-

142
00:09:20,360 --> 00:09:27,760
I mean, at the time everybody felt like they were going to die, but it was fun.

143
00:09:27,760 --> 00:09:36,000
How about waking up one morning and finding a bear ate all your food?

144
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:38,280
Not fun,

145
00:09:38,280 --> 00:09:45,200
No, very unpleasant at the time, but through the prism of memory and this kind

146
00:09:45,200 --> 00:09:51,480
of magical thing that happens, these are incredibly great memories.

147
00:09:51,480 --> 00:09:56,480
They are accomplishments and that was fun.

148
00:09:56,480 --> 00:10:01,800
So friends are fun and challenges are fun, and even dismal, awful challenges

149
00:10:01,800 --> 00:10:02,800
can be fun.

150
00:10:02,800 --> 00:10:04,880
So really great challenges,

151
00:10:04,880 --> 00:10:08,280
They are super fun.

152
00:10:08,280 --> 00:10:13,880
Independence is an important aspect of fun.

153
00:10:13,880 --> 00:10:19,560
I remember the intense sense of independence

154
00:10:19,560 --> 00:10:25,400
We felt, you know, as a kid went on a Saturday morning. we'd get on our

155
00:10:25,400 --> 00:10:28,480
bikes with three or four of our best buddies and we would head off for

156
00:10:28,480 --> 00:10:29,960
the day.

157
00:10:29,960 --> 00:10:33,800
That was just the best thing ever

158
00:10:33,800 --> 00:10:41,480
At 12 or 13,. with a bike, we had the world at our feet and we just

159
00:10:41,480 --> 00:10:44,600
had this whole kingdom that we could bike through.

160
00:10:44,600 --> 00:10:50,400
Now no one knew exactly where we were or exactly what we were doing or

161
00:10:50,400 --> 00:10:52,560
exactly when we'd be back.

162
00:10:52,560 --> 00:10:56,320
We were on our own and it was magical.

163
00:10:56,320 --> 00:11:00,240
We'd spend our money as we wanted, we would wear what we wanted to go,

164
00:11:00,240 --> 00:11:04,560
we would say what we wanted to say and we would get back when we

165
00:11:04,560 --> 00:11:08,720
wanted to get back, as long as it was somewhat close to the time that

166
00:11:08,720 --> 00:11:12,080
the street lights went on, which was the universal signal for heading

167
00:11:12,080 --> 00:11:13,080
for home.

168
00:11:13,080 --> 00:11:17,040
Yeah, it's not that we did these marvelous, incredible things.

169
00:11:17,040 --> 00:11:20,960
I mean, it was pretty humdrum, you know.

170
00:11:20,960 --> 00:11:23,880
We'd ride around on the bikes, maybe go into McDonald's and maybe

171
00:11:23,880 --> 00:11:28,280
be able to afford a thing of french fries or something like that

172
00:11:28,280 --> 00:11:33,000
and, you know, go to places that we already knew about. so that in

173
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:34,280
itself wasn't the fun part.

174
00:11:34,280 --> 00:11:37,480
The fun part was is we were on our own and we got to do it by

175
00:11:37,520 --> 00:11:41,320
ourselves, and it was just a heady, incredible experience.

176
00:11:41,320 --> 00:11:43,160
Do you remember that?

177
00:11:43,160 --> 00:11:47,200
So scouts need to have some independence.

178
00:11:47,200 --> 00:11:51,680
They need to be on their own to the greatest extent possible to

179
00:11:51,680 --> 00:11:54,840
experience a sense of real independence.

180
00:11:54,840 --> 00:11:57,880
That is tremendously fun.

181
00:11:57,880 --> 00:12:02,320
Fun is not usually a carefully mapped out or managed experience.

182
00:12:02,320 --> 00:12:05,200
It's usually a little chaotic and unpredictable.

183
00:12:05,240 --> 00:12:09,040
So go back to being that 12-year-old self, and maybe a

184
00:12:09,040 --> 00:12:13,160
few years younger than that, and remember birthday parties.

185
00:12:13,160 --> 00:12:20,000
Now, maybe I'm all alone on this, but I remember birthday

186
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:23,680
parties as not being a whole heck of a lot of fun.

187
00:12:23,680 --> 00:12:26,640
I mean, they could be really miserable.

188
00:12:26,640 --> 00:12:29,560
So you go there, you have all your friends,

189
00:12:29,560 --> 00:12:32,200
So that's one of the elements of fun.

190
00:12:32,200 --> 00:12:33,600
You have cake

191
00:12:33,640 --> 00:12:37,440
If you're the birthday boy or girl, you get presents,

192
00:12:37,440 --> 00:12:41,920
But it was all kind of controlled and presented by adults

193
00:12:41,920 --> 00:12:47,880
and I was supposed to react in predictable ways and my

194
00:12:47,880 --> 00:12:50,400
friends were supposed to react in predictable ways

195
00:12:50,400 --> 00:12:54,720
And somehow it could just be awful.

196
00:12:54,720 --> 00:12:57,440
Not every birthday was awful, but some of them-

197
00:12:57,440 --> 00:12:58,600
Oh, you're very,

198
00:12:58,600 --> 00:13:02,040
I mean some of them- were not happy days.

199
00:13:02,040 --> 00:13:05,800
I think every one of us can remember a similar experience,

200
00:13:05,800 --> 00:13:08,959
All the elements of fun, but it was so highly engineered

201
00:13:08,959 --> 00:13:11,319
It just didn't work out to be fun at all.

202
00:13:11,319 --> 00:13:15,680
Fun is like one of these things that it seems like if you

203
00:13:15,680 --> 00:13:20,480
make fun your goal, you say, well, this will be fun.

204
00:13:20,480 --> 00:13:23,640
It has a really good chance of not being fun

205
00:13:23,640 --> 00:13:26,839
If you make hanging out with your friends and being

206
00:13:26,839 --> 00:13:31,480
challenged and having some independence- your goal.

207
00:13:31,800 --> 00:13:34,480
you got a better and even chance of it being something

208
00:13:34,480 --> 00:13:35,440
that is fun.

209
00:13:35,440 --> 00:13:37,040
So we're talking about fun and scouting.

210
00:13:37,040 --> 00:13:39,640
We aren't talking about matching tablecloths and napkins

211
00:13:39,640 --> 00:13:43,400
and paper plates and a piñata and a cake with candles

212
00:13:43,400 --> 00:13:44,240
and party favors.

213
00:13:44,240 --> 00:13:47,080
We're talking about friends and challenges and

214
00:13:47,080 --> 00:13:48,360
independence.

215
00:13:48,360 --> 00:13:53,240
If those three things are in a walk around the block,

216
00:13:53,240 --> 00:13:55,120
it will be fun.

217
00:13:55,120 --> 00:13:57,200
If they're not, in a trip halfway around the world

218
00:13:57,200 --> 00:14:00,160
to the great places, it won't be fun.

