We have several boys in our troop that have partial

244
00:15:35,120 --> 00:15:38,120
completions on several merit badges.

245
00:15:38,120 --> 00:15:39,720
Usually they are from summer camp.

246
00:15:39,720 --> 00:15:41,520
Some of them are from several years ago

247
00:15:41,520 --> 00:15:43,720
and the boys were not given blue cards

248
00:15:43,720 --> 00:15:46,320
But a report was sent containing all the merit badge

249
00:15:46,320 --> 00:15:47,820
information.

250
00:15:47,820 --> 00:15:50,320
Do the scouts need to find another merit badge

251
00:15:50,320 --> 00:15:53,020
counselor to complete the work?

252
00:15:53,020 --> 00:15:55,320
We live in a fairly small rural town

253
00:15:55,320 --> 00:15:58,020
and we do not have some of the merit badge counselors

254
00:15:58,020 --> 00:16:00,820
that match up with what the boys are missing.

255
00:16:00,820 --> 00:16:02,620
My advancement chair, a predecessor,

256
00:16:02,620 --> 00:16:05,320
would sometimes check off the missing requirement

257
00:16:05,320 --> 00:16:07,920
if it was something like you know:

258
00:16:07,920 --> 00:16:11,020
show a finished project to your merit badge counselor.

259
00:16:11,020 --> 00:16:13,320
Is that acceptable, or do all the requirements

260
00:16:13,320 --> 00:16:15,420
for merit badges have to be checked off

261
00:16:15,420 --> 00:16:18,120
by a merit badge counselor for that merit badge

262
00:16:18,120 --> 00:16:19,520
to get credit?

263
00:16:19,520 --> 00:16:22,820
I brought this up and my Wood Badge troop guide

264
00:16:22,820 --> 00:16:27,720
said that I have hit upon a touchy subject.

265
00:16:27,720 --> 00:16:29,720
Since advancement is part of my ticket,

266
00:16:29,720 --> 00:16:31,620
I want to know the right thing for my scouts.

267
00:16:31,620 --> 00:16:32,520
Any advice?

268
00:16:32,520 --> 00:16:35,420
Well, first of all, Pete, thanks for listening

269
00:16:35,420 --> 00:16:36,920
and thanks for getting in touch.

270
00:16:36,920 --> 00:16:38,120
Short answer

271
00:16:38,120 --> 00:16:39,320
Is an easy answer:

272
00:16:39,320 --> 00:16:42,220
No,

273
00:16:42,220 --> 00:16:44,520
It's not acceptable for anyone other than a counselor

274
00:16:44,520 --> 00:16:46,520
registered for the merit badge in question

275
00:16:46,520 --> 00:16:48,620
to certify its completion.

276
00:16:48,620 --> 00:16:50,820
Now, that's not my opinion,

277
00:16:50,820 --> 00:16:51,920
That's policy.

278
00:16:51,920 --> 00:16:53,620
I don't know why anybody would have told you

279
00:16:53,620 --> 00:16:55,320
that this is a touchy subject,

280
00:16:55,320 --> 00:16:58,420
as if there were different ways to interpret it.

281
00:16:58,420 --> 00:17:00,720
This is pretty much black and white policy.

282
00:17:00,720 --> 00:17:03,720
I understand the spirit of maybe helping

283
00:17:03,720 --> 00:17:05,020
a boy finish up a merit badge

284
00:17:05,020 --> 00:17:07,020
by signing those last few requirements,

285
00:17:07,020 --> 00:17:08,520
but if we do that,

286
00:17:08,520 --> 00:17:11,220
we're really stepping off the reservation.

287
00:17:11,220 --> 00:17:15,920
If you look at the new Guide to Advancement 2011

288
00:17:15,920 --> 00:17:19,320
and you look at Section 7,

289
00:17:19,320 --> 00:17:23,420
you will see a paragraph about partial completions.

290
00:17:23,420 --> 00:17:25,320
Let me read that to you real quickly.

291
00:17:25,320 --> 00:17:27,520
Scouts need not pass all requirements

292
00:17:28,520 --> 00:17:31,120
so they can get a second counselor if they need to.

293
00:17:31,120 --> 00:17:33,420
The application for the merit badge

294
00:17:33,420 --> 00:17:37,020
has a place to record what has been finished,

295
00:17:37,020 --> 00:17:39,620
a partial

296
00:17:39,620 --> 00:17:41,320
So yeah, on the blue card

297
00:17:41,320 --> 00:17:42,820
or the application for the merit badge,

298
00:17:42,820 --> 00:17:44,420
there's a little grid on the back

299
00:17:44,420 --> 00:17:46,120
and the counselor can fill out

300
00:17:46,120 --> 00:17:47,520
what a scout finished

301
00:17:47,520 --> 00:17:49,520
and then the scout can take that

302
00:17:49,520 --> 00:17:51,420
to the next counselor

303
00:17:51,420 --> 00:17:55,920
and use it to represent what was finished.

304
00:17:56,020 --> 00:17:57,320
You're saying, Pete,

305
00:17:57,320 --> 00:17:59,320
that you got some kind of a document

306
00:17:59,320 --> 00:18:00,420
from the scout camp.

307
00:18:00,420 --> 00:18:03,920
Well, basically it has the same effect.

308
00:18:03,920 --> 00:18:06,520
A subsequent counselor may choose

309
00:18:06,520 --> 00:18:08,820
not to accept partial work,

310
00:18:08,820 --> 00:18:10,220
but this should be rare.

311
00:18:10,220 --> 00:18:12,920
A scout, if he believes he has been treating unfairly,

312
00:18:12,920 --> 00:18:14,120
may work with a scout master

313
00:18:14,120 --> 00:18:15,820
to find another counselor.

314
00:18:15,820 --> 00:18:20,020
An example for the use of a signed partial

315
00:18:20,020 --> 00:18:22,420
would be to take it to camp

316
00:18:22,420 --> 00:18:25,020
as a proof of prerequisites.

317
00:18:25,020 --> 00:18:27,520
and partials have no expiration

318
00:18:27,520 --> 00:18:31,520
except the 18th birthday. okay,

319
00:18:31,520 --> 00:18:35,120
So there's nothing in that reading

320
00:18:35,120 --> 00:18:36,720
that permits anyone

321
00:18:36,720 --> 00:18:38,020
but a registered counselor

322
00:18:38,020 --> 00:18:41,420
to certify completion of a merit badge.

323
00:18:41,420 --> 00:18:43,320
You know, once again, it's not a touchy subject,

324
00:18:43,320 --> 00:18:45,420
It's clear black and white policy.

325
00:18:45,420 --> 00:18:46,620
The shortcut of someone

326
00:18:46,620 --> 00:18:48,020
who is not a registered counselor

327
00:18:48,020 --> 00:18:50,220
signing off the last few requirements

328
00:18:50,220 --> 00:18:51,920
simply isn't acceptable.

329
00:18:51,920 --> 00:18:53,420
It all stops and starts

330
00:18:53,420 --> 00:18:55,320
with the guide to advancement.

331
00:18:55,320 --> 00:18:56,620
if it's not in there,

332
00:18:56,620 --> 00:18:57,720
It's not correct.

333
00:18:57,720 --> 00:18:58,820
So listen, folks,

334
00:18:58,820 --> 00:19:01,120
My experience is that you know

335
00:19:01,120 --> 00:19:04,120
you've done some things one way in the past

336
00:19:04,120 --> 00:19:06,520
and you go to something like the guide to advancement

337
00:19:06,520 --> 00:19:08,720
and you look for supporting language to say,

338
00:19:08,720 --> 00:19:11,320
oh well, yeah, of course this is the way that we do it.

339
00:19:11,320 --> 00:19:15,320
But hey, sometimes people just get things upside down

340
00:19:15,320 --> 00:19:16,220
or backwards or wrong,

341
00:19:16,220 --> 00:19:19,420
Not because they're horrible, awful people,

342
00:19:19,420 --> 00:19:21,320
It's just that they didn't know.

343
00:19:21,320 --> 00:19:22,620
So when you ask and you know,

344
00:19:22,620 --> 00:19:24,320
and you see that there's a change,

345
00:19:24,320 --> 00:19:26,520
that's the change that needs to be made.

346
00:19:26,520 --> 00:19:28,920
Now what I would recommend, Pete,

347
00:19:28,920 --> 00:19:31,520
I wouldn't revisit any of the merit badges

348
00:19:31,520 --> 00:19:32,720
where this has already happened.

349
00:19:32,720 --> 00:19:34,620
That's water under the bridge.

350
00:19:34,620 --> 00:19:37,720
Let's just not ever do this again in the future.

351
00:19:37,720 --> 00:19:39,320
So you're in a small rural town.

352
00:19:39,320 --> 00:19:43,320
You don't have all 130 merit badge counselors

353
00:19:43,320 --> 00:19:44,220
or whatever it is now.

354
00:19:44,220 --> 00:19:47,420
Well, you know that shouldn't be that big of a problem.

355
00:19:47,420 --> 00:19:49,720
Your best way forward, in my opinion,

356
00:19:49,720 --> 00:19:51,920
is you get the approved counselor list

357
00:19:52,020 --> 00:19:53,620
from your council

358
00:19:53,620 --> 00:19:57,420
And remember, folks, that councils have to approve

359
00:19:57,420 --> 00:19:59,120
merit badge counselors.

360
00:19:59,120 --> 00:20:00,820
You can't just approve them in a unit

361
00:20:00,820 --> 00:20:02,820
or something like that.

362
00:20:02,820 --> 00:20:04,520
If there's only one or two requirements

363
00:20:04,520 --> 00:20:07,020
to clear up the badge

364
00:20:07,020 --> 00:20:11,320
and they're kind of, you know, show me a report

365
00:20:11,320 --> 00:20:13,920
or tell me what reply you received on a letter,

366
00:20:13,920 --> 00:20:17,820
or show me a project, you know

367
00:20:17,820 --> 00:20:19,520
the counselor may be happy to do this

368
00:20:19,520 --> 00:20:21,620
via email or over the phone.

369
00:20:21,620 --> 00:20:23,920
And if that happens again,

370
00:20:23,920 --> 00:20:26,420
make sure we apply youth protection measures

371
00:20:26,420 --> 00:20:29,520
that are in place, like copying third parties

372
00:20:29,520 --> 00:20:32,320
on emails and things.

373
00:20:32,320 --> 00:20:34,420
And if you're in a rural situation,

374
00:20:34,420 --> 00:20:36,420
my guess is that counselors in your area

375
00:20:36,420 --> 00:20:39,020
have kind of figured out how to make things work

376
00:20:39,020 --> 00:20:43,220
for rural scouts without anybody having to be put out too much.

377
00:20:43,220 --> 00:20:47,220
So, Pete, I hope that helps some of this kind of bad news.

378
00:20:47,220 --> 00:20:49,920
The encouraging thing is you want to do things the right way.

379
00:20:49,920 --> 00:20:51,220
That's always great,

380
